title: 'FIXED: absorb worktree concurrency (T-2026-06-23-003) — git-archive materialization, the parallel-agent gate'
summary: 'Implemented + shipped Cid''s round-2 fix for the absorb worktree concurrency bug — the literal gate to any parallel-agent path. absorb''s real-ref branch now materializes a ref''s tree via `git archive | tar` into a temp dir (no `git worktree`, no `.git/worktrees` lock) instead of `git worktree add/remove`, so concurrent absorbs against one repo are safe. The cold git<2.38 merge-tree fallback (the one remaining worktree user) is serialized per-repo by a new #repo-lock mutex. Proof: flipped vitest fileParallelism:false→true and the full 104-test suite passes (twice) under the exact parallelism that used to flake. Aegis security-reviewed (verdict ship-with-nits → both must-fixes landed).'
